# OCaml opam environment

Before running `dune`, `ocaml`, `opam install`, or other OCaml tooling for this repo, instantiate the project opam environment:

```bash
export OPAMROOT="/lm/users/arul/.opam"
eval "$(OPAMROOT="$OPAMROOT" opam env --switch=5.5.0)"
```

## Makefile defaults

The root `Makefile` uses the same values for `make ocaml` and `make ocaml-run`:

- `OPAMROOT ?= /lm/users/arul/.opam`
- `OCAML_SWITCH ?= 5.5.0`

Prefer `make ocaml` / `make ocaml-run` from the repo root when possible; they apply opam env automatically.

## First-time setup

If switch `5.5.0` does not exist:

```bash
export OPAMROOT="/lm/users/arul/.opam"
opam switch create 5.5.0 ocaml-base-compiler.5.5.0
eval "$(OPAMROOT="$OPAMROOT" opam env --switch=5.5.0)"
opam install dune ctypes ctypes-foreign
```

## Build flow

1. `make kron-lib` — generate Futhark C library and copy to `ocaml/thuli/kron.c`
2. `make ocaml` — build the OCaml library under `ocaml/`
3. `make ocaml-run` — build and run `ocaml/bin/main.exe`

Run `make kron-lib` before `make ocaml` when `programs/kron.fut` or library `.fut` sources change.

## Verification

After editing OCaml files, run `make ocaml`. If runtime behavior changed, also run `make ocaml-run`.

Do not assume a global/default opam switch; always set `OPAMROOT` and use switch `5.5.0`.
